# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/chain_hollowstar_acts.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event hs_lake_breathes
# en: The Lake Breathes
title [6ab0a7] = 湖在呼吸
# en: At supper the lake outside the tall windows goes white in one breath, and every candle in the Great Hall leans toward it. Far under the water a bell tolls. Professor Thorne's spoon freezes into his soup. The headmistress rises. "A cold current," she says pleasantly. "Eat." Then the lake breathes out, and is water again. Nobody eats.
text [631628] = 晚餐时，高窗外的湖在一口气间变白，大礼堂里的每一支蜡烛都朝它倾斜。湖水深处，一口钟响了。索恩教授的勺子冻在了汤里。院长站了起来。“一股冷流而已，”她和颜悦色地说，“吃饭。”然后湖呼出那口气，又变回了水。没有人吃得下。
# en: The Great Hall at supper, every head turned to the tall windows, the lake beyond them gone white with sudden frost.
scene [96af25] = 晚餐时的大礼堂，所有人都转头望向高窗，窗外的湖面骤然覆上一层白霜。
# en: Run down to the shore
opt.left.label [3bc011] = 跑到湖边去
# en: The shore is soaked and freezing, and the reeds are white to the root. Old Maud is already there with a lantern, staring at the water. "Last time it did that, I lost a friend," she says, not quite to you. Then she sends you to bed, sharply, and you go.
opt.left.say.1 [88d600] = 湖岸又湿又冷，芦苇从根到梢都白了。老莫德已经提着灯在那里了，盯着湖水。“上一次它这样，我失去了一个朋友。”她说，不太像是在对你说。然后她厉声叫你回去睡觉，你就回去了。
# en: Follow Thorne out of the hall
opt.right.label [a49e19] = 跟着索恩离开大礼堂
# en: Thorne leaves his frozen soup and walks straight to the library archive, fast for a man of his age. You hear the vault door slam. You lie awake wondering what he went down there to read.
opt.right.say.1 [5176f6] = 索恩撇下冻住的汤，径直走向图书馆档案室，以他的年纪走得飞快。你听见金库的门砰地关上。你躺着睡不着，琢磨他到底下去读什么。

@event hs_silver_rings
# en: Silver at Supper
title [65d7d8] = 晚餐桌上的银戒
# en: At supper you notice three identical silver rings at the high table: on the headmistress, on Professor Thorne and on Old Maud's earthy hand. After curfew, from your window, you see all three walking the lakeshore with lanterns, stopping at the foot of each tower in turn.
text [0e82e1] = 晚餐时，你注意到主宾席上有三枚一模一样的银戒指：一枚戴在院长手上，一枚在索恩教授手上，还有一枚在老莫德那双沾着泥土的手上。宵禁之后，你从窗口望见他们三人提着灯笼沿湖岸走，在每座塔脚下依次停步。
# en: The Great Hall at supper, candlelight catching three identical silver rings on three very different hands at the high table.
scene [7eebf1] = 晚餐时的大礼堂，烛光照亮主宾席上三只截然不同的手上三枚一模一样的银戒指。
# en: Follow them down
opt.left.label [088fbe] = 跟下去看看
# en: You shadow them from tower to tower. At each one they lay a palm on the stone and wait. At the last, Maud takes her hand away and blows on her fingers as if the wall were ice.
opt.left.say.1 [ec6d76] = 你从一座塔跟到另一座塔。每到一处，他们都把手掌贴在石墙上，静静等着。到了最后一座，莫德把手收回来，对着指尖呵气，仿佛那面墙是冰做的。
# en: A lantern swings toward you. "Hm," says Professor Thorne. "Bed." He doesn't report you, which somehow feels worse.
opt.left.say.2 [c0b820] = 一盏灯笼朝你转过来。“嗯。”索恩教授说，“睡觉去。”他没有上报你，不知为何这反而更难受。
# en: Draw the curtains
opt.right.label [899463] = 拉上窗帘
# en: You sleep well, mostly. In the morning the rings are still there at breakfast, and nobody at the high table looks as if they slept at all.
opt.right.say.1 [b6139e] = 你睡得还算不错。第二天早餐时，那几枚戒指还在，而主宾席上没有一个人看起来睡过觉。

@event hs_seraphine_towers
# en: Seven, Then Six
title [257255] = 七座，然后六座
# en: Seraphine is on the observatory balcony, counting towers on her fingers. "Seven," she says. "Seven. Six, and then… no. Seven, for now." She looks at you as if you had arrived a little early. "What month is it? I lose track around the… you know."
text [a96e33] = 瑟拉芬站在观星台的阳台上，掰着手指数塔。“七座，”她说，“七座。六座，然后……不。七座，暂时。”她看着你，仿佛你来得稍微早了一点。“现在是几月？我总是在……你知道的那个地方，弄丢日子。”
# en: A seer on the observatory balcony at night, counting the academy's towers on her fingers, one finger held back.
scene [34ef65] = 夜里观星台的阳台上，一位预言者掰着手指数学院的塔，有一根手指迟迟没有伸出来。
# en: "Which one goes out?"
opt.left.label [a243d5] = “哪一座会熄灭？”
# en: She points, then frowns at her own hand. "That one. Or the one next to it. Next year, I think. Not the seventh; nobody's lit the seventh for a hundred years." She doesn't remember saying it the next morning, but you do.
opt.left.say.1 [f52252] = 她指了一下，又对着自己的手皱起眉。“那一座。或者旁边那座。明年吧，我想。不是第七座；第七座已经一百年没人点灯了。”第二天早上她已经不记得说过这话，但你记得。
# en: "It's {month}. Evening."
opt.right.label [1c7b30] = “现在是{month}，傍晚。”
# en: She lets out a long breath and sits down on the cold stone. "Thank you. I was halfway into a winter." You stay until she is sure which one she's in.
opt.right.say.1 [1f863d] = 她长长地呼出一口气，在冰凉的石头上坐了下来。“谢谢。我已经半只脚踏进冬天了。”你一直陪着她，直到她确定自己身在哪个季节。

@event hs_ilse_arrives
# en: A Storm at the Gate
title [d881d0] = 门前的风暴
# en: At noon a snowstorm walks in through the academy gate, with a girl in white furs at the middle of it. Kael drops his books. "Go home, Ilse." "Make me." They shout at each other across the courtyard in Northern, and the fountain between them cracks in half. Half the school is watching. Then she turns on her heel and goes, down the road to the village.
text [eec352] = 正午，一场暴风雪从学院大门走了进来，正中间是一个穿白裘的女孩。凯尔的书掉在了地上。“回家去，伊尔泽。”“有本事你让我回。”他们隔着庭院用北境话对吼，两人之间的喷泉裂成了两半。半个学校都在看。然后她一转身走了，沿着大路往村子去。
# en: A snowstorm falling on one girl in white furs in the middle of a sunny courtyard, a pale young man facing her, students scattering, a cracked fountain between them.
scene [c05a43] = 阳光明媚的庭院正中，一场暴风雪只落在一个穿白裘的女孩身上，一个苍白的年轻人面对着她，学生们四散奔逃，两人之间是一座裂开的喷泉。
# en: Go after her
opt.left.label [7ddfb6] = 追上她
# en: Kael catches your sleeve. "Don't. She's here for the door, not for me." He lets go when you don't stop. By the time you reach the road the snow has stopped too, and there's only a line of frozen footprints toward the bakery.
opt.left.say.1 [6976ac] = 凯尔拽住你的袖子。“别去。她是为那扇门来的，不是为我。”你没停下，他就松了手。等你走到大路上，雪也停了，只剩一行冻住的脚印通向面包房。
# en: Stay with Kael
opt.right.label [2f5601] = 留在凯尔身边
# en: You pick up his books. He stands looking at the broken fountain until the bell goes. "My sister," he says at last. "She's taken a room above the bakery. She isn't here to visit."
opt.right.say.1 [059ef4] = 你帮他捡起书。他一直站着看那座裂开的喷泉，直到上课铃响。“我妹妹，”他终于开口，“她在面包房楼上租了间屋子。她不是来探亲的。”

@event hs_frost_ring
# en: Things Come Ashore
title [1186a4] = 它们上岸了
# en: {season == "winter": A still, starless night|A warm night}, and a ring of frost as wide as the Great Hall has formed in the middle of the lake. Far below, the bell tolls, and tolls. Then things climb out of the ring onto the shore: shapes of frost and whispers, walking like people who have forgotten how. The headmistress stands alone at the waterline with a lantern, talking to the lake.
text [bc66df] = {season == "winter": 一个寂静无星的夜晚|一个温暖的夜晚}，湖中央出现了一个和大礼堂一样宽的霜环。深处的钟响了，一下又一下。接着有东西从霜环里爬上了岸：由霜与低语构成的形体，走路的样子像是忘了该怎么走路的人。院长独自提着灯站在水边，对着湖说话。
# en: The Mirror Lake on a warm night, a perfect white ring of frost on the water, figures of frost and whispers climbing onto the shore, a tall woman with a lantern facing them.
scene [e742bc] = 温暖夜晚的镜湖，水面上一个完美的白色霜环，由霜与低语构成的身影爬上岸，一个提灯的高个子女人面对着它们。
# en: Meet them on the shore
opt.fight.label [67179b] = 在岸边迎击它们
# en: Combat. Kael fights beside you, if he's your ally.
opt.fight.hint [5999d9] = 战斗。如果凯尔是你的盟友，他会和你并肩作战。
# en: Kael's frost and your spells meet the first of them on the shingle, and it comes apart into snow and a sound like someone saying your name. The rest turn back to the water. Under the ice, as it closes, you hear the bell's note clearly for the first time.
opt.fight.say.1 [bd5e29] = 凯尔的霜和你的咒语在卵石滩上迎上了第一个，它散成了雪，还有一个像是有人在念你名字的声音。其余的转身回到水里。冰面合拢时，你第一次清楚地听见了那口钟的音。
# en: It walks through your spell as if it were weather and puts a cold hand on your chest, and you can't breathe for a long moment. Kael drags you back up the shingle. When you can see again, the ring has closed and the shapes are gone.
opt.fight.say.2 [2a6599] = 它像穿过天气一样穿过你的咒语，把一只冰冷的手按在你胸口，你好一阵喘不过气。凯尔把你拖回卵石滩上。等你能看清时，霜环已经合拢，那些形体也不见了。
# en: Your spell meets the first of them on the shingle, and it comes apart into snow and a sound like someone saying your name. The rest turn back to the water. Under the ice, as it closes, you hear the bell's note clearly for the first time.
opt.fight.say.3 [7285db] = 你的咒语在卵石滩上迎上了第一个，它散成了雪，还有一个像是有人在念你名字的声音。其余的转身回到水里。冰面合拢时，你第一次清楚地听见了那口钟的音。
# en: It walks through your spell as if it were weather and puts a cold hand on your chest, and you can't breathe for a long moment. When you can see again, the ring has closed, the shapes are gone, and the headmistress is helping you up.
opt.fight.say.4 [5386b7] = 它像穿过天气一样穿过你的咒语，把一只冰冷的手按在你胸口，你好一阵喘不过气。等你能看清时，霜环已经合拢，那些形体也不见了，院长正扶你起来。
# en: Watch what she does
opt.watch.label [29f82d] = 看她要做什么
# en: Guile. She doesn't like an audience.
opt.watch.hint [592c3d] = 诡计。她不喜欢有人围观。
# en: She kneels and speaks to the water, slow and patient, the way you'd speak to a sleeping animal. The shapes stop on the shingle and listen. The ring shrinks, cracks, and is gone, and the bell under it rings one long note you'll know again anywhere.
opt.watch.say.1 [57fb5e] = 她跪下来对着湖水说话，缓慢而耐心，就像对一头熟睡的野兽说话。那些形体在卵石滩上停下来倾听。霜环缩小、碎裂、消失，下面的钟敲出一个长音，此后你在哪里都认得出它。
# en: "Good evening," she says, without turning round, as a shape of frost walks past her into the lake. "You are the third student this week. The other two asked questions." She tells you nothing, and remembers your name.
opt.watch.say.2 [92f8ce] = “晚上好。”她头也不回地说，一个霜之形体从她身边走进湖里。“这周你是第三个来的学生。另外两个问了问题。”她什么也没告诉你，但记住了你的名字。
# en: Get the first-years inside
opt.help.label [b5bef7] = 把一年级生带进屋
# en: Nobody will see what happens at the water.
opt.help.hint [c86325] = 没人会看见水边发生了什么。
# en: You run the length of the first-year tower banging on doors, and get forty children into the common room and the shutters closed. Something taps on the glass all night, very politely. In the morning there are wet footprints on the stairs, going up.
opt.help.say.1 [e756c0] = 你沿着一年级塔一路砸门，把四十个孩子赶进公共休息室，关上了百叶窗。整夜都有什么东西非常有礼貌地敲着玻璃。早上，楼梯上有湿脚印，一路往上。

@event hs_dark_tower
# en: The Tower That Went Dark
title [eb9204] = 熄灭的塔
# en: Mid-lecture, every lamp in the Lecture Tower goes out at once, and none of them will light again. In the morning there's a black star burned into the door of the Great Hall, still smoking, and half the lake has frozen {season == "winter": black and glassy, harder than any winter ice|weeks before any frost}, in a sheet that ends in a clean edge, as if cut. Out on it, at dawn, someone in black furs is walking away.
text [4af36c] = 课上到一半，讲堂塔里的每一盏灯同时熄灭，再也点不亮了。第二天早上，大礼堂的门上烙着一颗黑星，还在冒烟；湖已冻住了一半，{season == "winter": 冻得乌黑如玻璃，比任何冬天的冰都硬|比任何霜冻都早了好几周}，冰面边缘齐整，像是被切出来的。黎明时，冰上有个穿黑裘的人正在走远。
# en: An academy tower standing black against the night sky among its lit neighbours, a black star burned into a great wooden door, and below them a lake half-covered in ice.
scene [d4a9f6] = 一座学院塔楼漆黑地矗立在夜空下，周围的塔都亮着灯，一扇巨大的木门上烙着一颗黑星，下方的湖一半盖着冰。
# en: Go after the figure on the ice
opt.left.label [3ab56b] = 追冰上那个人影
# en: Nerve. The ice is thinner than it looks.
opt.left.hint [25bd25] = 胆量。冰比看上去薄。
# en: You follow the footprints to the middle of the ice, where they simply stop. Under your boots the ice is clear as glass. Far down, something round and dark sits on the lakebed, and a glow runs along its rim. Then the glow turns, slowly, as if to look up.
opt.left.say.1 [01453c] = 你跟着脚印走到冰面中央，脚印就在那里断了。你脚下的冰像玻璃一样清澈。深处，湖底卧着一个又圆又黑的东西，边缘流动着一圈光。然后那圈光慢慢转动，像是要抬头看。
# en: The ice groans and a crack races past your feet. You scramble back to the shore soaked to the knee, and a prefect writes your name down very slowly. The figure in black furs never once looks back.
opt.left.say.2 [a926ea] = 冰面呻吟着，一道裂缝从你脚边飞窜而过。你连滚带爬回到岸上，膝盖以下都湿透了，一个级长慢吞吞地记下了你的名字。那个穿黑裘的人影一次也没有回头。
# en: Carry lamps for the prefects
opt.right.label [6083a9] = 帮级长们搬灯
# en: You spend the night carrying lamps up the Lecture Tower stairs. Every one goes out at the doorway. The first-years have started sleeping in their clothes. From her window across the courtyard, the headmistress watches you try.
opt.right.say.1 [66a8f5] = 你整夜提着灯爬讲堂塔的楼梯。每一盏灯一到门口就灭。一年级生已经开始和衣而睡了。院长在庭院对面的窗口看着你一次次尝试。

@event hs_maud_locks
# en: Maud Has Seen Ice Before
title [b78fd5] = 莫德见过这种冰
# en: At Maud's gate the headmistress is saying, quite pleasantly, "Keep the young ones out of it, Maud." "No," says Maud, "and you know why." The headmistress walks away very straight. Maud pushes a mug of tea at you. "{season == "winter": It doesn't freeze like that, dearie, not even in winter|The lake doesn't freeze this time of year, dearie}. Sixty years ago it did, and three of us went down. Sit. Or ask."
text [84a878] = 莫德的院门口，院长正和气地说：“别让年轻人掺和进来，莫德。”“不，”莫德说，“你知道为什么。”院长走开了，背挺得笔直。莫德把一杯茶推给你。“{season == "winter": 它不会那样结冰的，亲爱的，冬天也不会|一年里的这个时候，湖是不会结冰的，亲爱的}。六十年前它结过一次，我们三个下去了。坐下吧。要么就问。”
# en: An old woman wrapped in a shawl on her cottage step, two mugs steaming beside her, a tall woman in dark robes walking stiffly away down the path, a half-frozen lake beyond.
scene [d4760c] = 一个裹着披肩的老妇人坐在小屋门阶上，身边两杯热气腾腾的茶，一个穿深色长袍的高个子女人僵硬地沿着小路走远，远处是半冻的湖。
# en: Sit with her
opt.left.label [654e0a] = 陪她坐着
# en: You drink your tea and watch the ice. She hums something old. When the mugs are empty she squeezes your hand. "That was the right one," she says, and you'll only understand why much later.
opt.left.say.1 [7b5291] = 你喝着茶，看着冰面。她哼着一支老调子。杯子空了，她捏了捏你的手。“选对了。”她说。你要过很久才明白为什么。
# en: Ask what's holding it shut
opt.right.label [8d8004] = 问是什么把门锁住
# en: "Seven towers, seven locks, one in each," she says. "When a tower goes dark, so does its lock." She looks at the Lecture Tower. "Locks can be mended. They need hands, and they need a key, and she knows it."
opt.right.say.1 [bcb6f3] = “七座塔，七把锁，每座一把，”她说，“一座塔黑了，它的锁也就哑了。”她看着讲堂塔。“锁是能修的。要有手，还要有钥匙，这她清楚。”

@event hs_two_shadows
# en: Two Wands on the Ice
title [412c93] = 冰上的两根魔杖
# en: At dusk the headmistress and Kael walk out onto the frozen half of the lake from opposite shores and meet in the middle. Kael's voice carries all the way to the towers: "You'll seal it with students standing in the door!" Hers never rises, and carries anyway: "Better than your mother's way." Both wands come up. For a long moment nobody moves. Then she lowers hers first, and they part in silence.
text [dae66a] = 黄昏时，院长和凯尔从两岸走上湖面结冰的那一半，在中央相遇。凯尔的声音一直传到塔楼：“你要把门封上，连站在门口的学生一起！”她的声音从不提高，却也传了过来：“总比你母亲的办法好。”两根魔杖都举了起来。很长一段时间谁也没动。然后她先放下了魔杖，两人沉默着分开了。
# en: Dusk on a half-frozen lake, two figures facing each other in the middle of the ice with wands raised, one holding a lantern, the dark tower behind them.
scene [08771e] = 黄昏时半冻的湖，两个身影在冰面中央举着魔杖对峙，其中一人提着灯，身后是那座黑塔。
# en: Ask Kael what they said
opt.left.label [91a8f0] = 问凯尔他们说了什么
# en: "She wants the door shut her way. I want it shut mine." He stirs his tea until it freezes. "She asked about you. So did I. Don't make that face. You'll be asked."
opt.left.say.1 [3a12d8] = “她想按她的办法关上那扇门。我想按我的。”他搅着茶，直到茶冻住。“她问起了你。我也问了。别做那种表情。会有人来问你的。”
# en: Ask the headmistress
opt.right.label [733de3] = 去问校长
# en: "We disagree about method," she says, "and agree about the door." She studies you as if you were a chess problem. "Expect an invitation. Possibly two. Choose with your eyes open." Kael, across the hall, sees you leave her tower.
opt.right.say.1 [7d491d] = “我们在方法上有分歧，”她说，“在门的问题上意见一致。”她打量着你，像在研究一道棋局。“等着收邀请吧。可能是两份。睁大眼睛再选。”大厅另一头，凯尔看见你从她的塔里出来。

@event hs_choosing_sides
# en: Two Invitations
title [b97cfd] = 两份邀请
# en: Two invitations, both in front of the whole refectory. The headmistress, passing your table: "My study, after supper. Come alone. There will be chess." And Kael, not ten seconds later, loud enough for her to hear: "She wants you in her circle. I know the door from the other side. Come with us." Every head in the hall turns to you.
text [10ee8c] = 两份邀请，都当着整个膳堂的面。院长经过你的桌边：“晚饭后来我书房。一个人来。会有棋下。”不到十秒，凯尔就开口了，声音大得足够让她听见：“她想让你进她的圈子。我从门的另一边认识那扇门。跟我们走吧。”整个大厅的人都转过头来看你。
# en: A crowded refectory gone quiet, a student at a table between a tall woman in dark robes and a pale young man, both waiting for an answer.
scene [d5678c] = 拥挤的膳堂安静下来，一个学生坐在桌边，一边是穿深色长袍的高个子女人，一边是苍白的年轻人，两人都在等一个答复。
# en: Join the headmistress's circle
opt.wardens.label [d0d300] = 加入院长的圈子
# en: The Wardens: old rules, old wards.
opt.wardens.hint [8082aa] = 守望者：古老的规矩，古老的护界。
# en: She beats you at chess in eleven moves, then tells you about the seal while she resets the board. "Rings are for people who have stood on the ice," she says. "Until then, you have my door."
opt.wardens.say.1 [1f494e] = 她用十一步棋赢了你，一边重新摆棋盘，一边给你讲封印的事。“戒指是给站上过冰面的人的。”她说，“在那之前，我的门为你开着。”
# en: Stand with the Dumonts
opt.dumonts.label [1cf610] = 站在杜蒙兄妹一边
# en: Kael's way, against his own family.
opt.dumonts.hint [3d8ab6] = 凯尔的路，与他自己的家族为敌。
# en: "Not my family," Kael says, to the whole hall. "Us." He teaches you to hold a ward in a wind that wants your fingers. His hands are cold. They are steadier than yours.
opt.dumonts.say.1 [42717e] = “不是我的家族，”凯尔对着整个大厅说，“是我们。”他教你在一阵想把你手指吹掉的风里稳住护界。他的手很冷。比你的稳。
# en: Go my own way
opt.self.label [90c2bc] = 走我自己的路
# en: Nobody's circle. Nobody's help.
opt.self.hint [06bcd0] = 不入任何圈子，也没人帮忙。
# en: You thank them both, out loud, and keep your own notes in your own cipher. It's lonelier than you expected. Both of them, you notice, keep an eye on you anyway.
opt.self.say.1 [725a6a] = 你大声谢过他们两人，然后用自己的密码记自己的笔记。这比你想象的孤独。你注意到，他们俩还是都在留意着你。
# en: Stay out of it
opt.none.label [03d24a] = 置身事外
# en: It isn't your door.
opt.none.hint [4c3c5a] = 那不是你的门。
# en: You turn both invitations down. Kael nods as if he expected it. The headmistress's note simply says, the next morning, "Understood. Mind the ice."
opt.none.say.1 [80761e] = 你婉拒了两份邀请。凯尔点点头，像是早就料到。第二天早上，院长的字条上只写着：“明白了。当心冰面。”

@event hs_last_winter
# en: The Last Winter Before
title [77b708] = 最后一个冬天之前
# en: The Lecture Tower has been dark for a year, and the lake freezes overnight in circles now. In spring the seal will be at its weakest. In the same week, one after another, they come and say it plainly: they'll stand with you beneath the lake, if you'll have them. You have one winter, and evenings enough for one of them.
text [d16c82] = 讲堂塔已经黑了一年，如今湖面一夜之间就会冻出一圈圈的冰。到了春天，封印会是最弱的时候。同一周里，他们一个接一个来找你，把话说得明明白白：如果你愿意，他们会在湖底与你并肩。你只有一个冬天，晚上的时间只够陪其中一个人。
# en: Lantern light in a frost-rimed window, the frozen edge of the lake beyond it, a student's desk covered in maps of seven towers.
scene [e5b843] = 结霜的窗户里透出灯笼的光，窗外是湖面冰冻的边缘，学生的书桌上铺满了七座塔的地图。
# en: Train with Kael on the ice
opt.kael.label [f6da05] = 和凯尔在冰上训练
# en: He'll come down with you, and fight beside you.
opt.kael.hint [23f740] = 他会和你一起下去，并肩作战。
# en: He drills you on the ice until you can hold a ward with numb hands. "Again," he says, and then, quietly, "Good." You will remember that he said it.
opt.kael.say.1 [e69c38] = 他在冰上一遍遍操练你，直到你能用冻僵的手撑住护界。“再来。”他说，然后轻声补了一句：“很好。”你会记得他说过这句话。
# en: Mend wards with Maud
opt.maud.label [7044a1] = 和莫德修补护界
# en: She'll come down with you, and knows the founders' wall.
opt.maud.hint [5b909a] = 她会和你一起下去，她认得创始者之墙。
# en: You walk the towers with her, tracing old wards back into the stone. "Your hands are steadier than mine were," she says, and doesn't say whose hands she means.
opt.maud.say.1 [9b7f55] = 你陪她走遍七塔，把古老的护界一笔一笔描回石头里。“你的手比我当年的稳。”她说，却没说她指的是谁的手。
# en: Study with the headmistress
opt.isolde.label [d9f337] = 跟院长学习
# en: She'll come down with you; you'll know the founders' words.
opt.isolde.hint [9053dc] = 她会和你一起下去；你会熟记创始者的话。
# en: You lose at chess every evening and learn the founders' words between moves. Once you nearly win. Her short, delighted laugh is the warmest sound you hear all winter.
opt.isolde.say.1 [627308] = 每个傍晚你都输棋，在落子之间学会了创始者的咒文。有一次你差点赢了。她那短促而欣喜的笑声，是你整个冬天听过最温暖的声音。
# en: Spar with Ilse at the shore
opt.ilse.label [b13627] = 和伊尔泽在湖边对练
# en: She'll come down with you, and fight beside you.
opt.ilse.hint [355c01] = 她会和你一起下去，并肩作战。
# en: She knocks you into the snow eleven times. The twelfth time you don't fall, and she looks at you as if you had done a trick she has never learned the counter to.
opt.ilse.say.1 [86c9c1] = 她把你打进雪里十一次。第十二次你没有倒下，她看着你，仿佛你使出了一招她从没学过怎么破解的戏法。
# en: Rest while you still can
opt.alone.label [639301] = 趁还能休息就休息
# en: A quiet winter. No new training, but rested.
opt.alone.hint [ead4d4] = 一个安静的冬天。没有新的训练，但精力充沛。
# en: You sleep, you eat, you read novels with no doors in them. It's the kindest winter you've had in years, and you can feel the lake getting colder anyway.
opt.alone.say.1 [7e93f5] = 你睡觉，吃饭，读那些里面没有门的小说。这是你多年来最温柔的一个冬天，可你还是感觉得到湖水在一天天变冷。

@event hs_ilse_door
# en: What Ilse Was Taught
title [8a9ef8] = 伊尔泽学过的东西
# en: Ilse draws a circle in the snow with her wand, then a smaller one inside it. "This is the door," she says. "I have drawn it every day since I was six. I have never seen it." She doesn't look up. "Ask me what they taught me to do. Or don't. I don't care which."
text [f6aa80] = 伊尔泽用魔杖在雪地上画了一个圆，又在里面画了一个小圆。“这就是那扇门。”她说，“我从六岁起每天都画它。我从没见过它。”她没有抬头。“问我他们教了我做什么。或者别问。我无所谓。”
# en: A young woman in white furs drawing a round door in the snow with the tip of a wand, a frozen lake behind her.
scene [1adcfd] = 一个身披白裘的年轻女子用魔杖尖在雪地上画一扇圆门，身后是冰封的湖。
# en: "What did they teach you?"
opt.left.label [ee8d4b] = “他们教了你什么？”
# en: She tells you, flatly, like a lesson recited: how to stand, what to say, where to put her hands. "They raised me to open it," she says. "Nobody asked me if I wanted to." Then, sharply: "Now you know. Don't look at me like that."
opt.left.say.1 [e300d4] = 她平板地讲给你听，像在背诵一堂课：怎么站，说什么，手放在哪里。“他们把我养大，就是为了让我打开它。”她说，“从没人问过我想不想。”然后她语气一冷：“现在你知道了。别用那种眼神看我。”
# en: "You don't have to tell me."
opt.right.label [194cf6] = “你不必告诉我。”
# en: She rubs the circle out with her boot. "Kindness," she says, as if naming a trick. "I haven't learned the counter to that one yet." She doesn't leave, though.
opt.right.say.1 [8dd039] = 她用靴子把那个圆抹掉。“善意。”她说，像在叫出一个戏法的名字，“这一招，我还没学会怎么破解。”不过，她没有走。
